=== The two ALERT results are this session's main finding ===

Both automation_log and performance_snapshots were listed in HARNESS.md §4.1
as "NO STATED EXPECTATION — new finding." Investigation (this session) found
BOTH are not merely unassigned — both have a live, universal write-path
defect that has made every insert attempt fail silently since inception:

--- automation_log ---
Live schema CHECK constraint on event_type:
  ARRAY['data_pull','analysis','recommendation','action_executed',
        'action_failed','alert','report','system']
Every writer in the codebase passes a DIFFERENT value:
  api/lib/execute-action-logic.js writeLog()  -> current.action_type / actionType
                                                  (e.g. 'pause_campaign', 'adjust_budget',
                                                  'add_negative_keyword', ...)
  api/cron-analyze.js       -> 'cron_analysis'
  api/cron-daily-stats.js   -> 'cron_daily_stats'
  api/cron-crm-sync.js      -> 'crm_sync'
  api/analyze-ads.js        -> 'analysis_run'
  api/meta-creative.js      -> 'creative_uploaded'
None of these six values are in the allowed list. None of the six call
sites destructure/check the `error` field Supabase returns on a CHECK
violation — all six are bare `await supabase.from('automation_log').insert(...)`
(execute-action-logic.js's writeLog wraps it in try/catch, but a CHECK
violation resolves with {error} set, it does not throw, so the catch never
fires either). Every write has always failed, silently, at every call site,
since the feature was built.

Consequence: any claim that automation_log evidences "Google Ads v23 read +
budget-change execution (validated live)" (PRIME-AGENCY-ROADMAP.md) cannot
be resting on this table — no row proving that has ever existed. Whatever
validation happened, it rested on other evidence (actions.status/result,
manual verification in the Google Ads UI, or similar), not this log.

--- performance_snapshots ---
Live schema: id, created_at, snapshot_date (NOT NULL), channel (NOT NULL,
CHECK IN google_ads/meta_ads/organic/combined), metrics (jsonb, default {}),
campaigns (jsonb, default []), account_id.

Write path (api/analyze-ads.js:302) inserts:
  { account_id, snapshot_at, google_data, meta_data, actions_created }
None of snapshot_at / google_data / meta_data / actions_created are columns
on the live table. snapshot_date and channel are NOT NULL and never
supplied. This insert cannot succeed against the real schema, and the call
site does not check the returned error (bare `await ...insert(...)`).

Read path (api/performance-snapshots.js) and the evaluate-outcomes.js
fallback (getSpendWithSource) both expect the SAME wrong shape
(data.google_data, data.meta_data, data.snapshot_at) — reader and writer
agree with each other, just not with the live table. Nobody has round-
tripped this table against its real schema.

Masking: evaluate-outcomes.js prefers campaign_daily_stats (111 rows live)
and only falls back to performance_snapshots when daily-stats data is
missing for a campaign/window — which has apparently not yet happened in
practice, so the broken fallback has never been exercised as the sole
source and its failure mode (returns spend:null, source:'none' — a safe,
non-crashing degradation) has gone unnoticed.

Test coverage: no test file exists for api/performance-snapshots.js.
tests/analyze-ads.test.js mocks Supabase entirely and asserts only that an
insert with account_id was attempted — never against the real column set —
which is why mocked tests have always passed while the live write has
always failed. This is the same class of gap as the memory note "verify
schema live, not from code" — mocks cannot catch live schema drift.

